# memory-tier-system

The memory tier system implements a specialized multi-level memory architecture with quantum-aware pattern management:

### Memory Tier Architecture
- Three distinct tiers: STM (Short-Term Memory), MTM (Medium-Term Memory), LTM (Long-Term Memory)
- Each tier maintains patterns based on coherence thresholds:
  - LTM: > 0.9 coherence
  - MTM: > 0.6 coherence 
  - STM: > 0.2 coherence

### Pattern Evolution & Migration
- Patterns evolve through tiers based on:
  - Quantum coherence scores
  - Stability metrics
  - Generation counts
  - Access frequency
  - Entanglement density
- Migration decisions use weighted scoring:
  - Coherence: 40%
  - Stability: 30%
  - Access frequency: 20%
  - Entanglement density: 10%

### Quantum State Management
- Maintains quantum coherence through:
  - Phase correlation tracking
  - Entanglement graph maintenance
  - Stability threshold monitoring
  - Entropy calculation
- Implements hysteresis to prevent oscillation between tiers

### Pattern Relationship Management
- Tracks pattern relationships using:
  - Spatial overlap in 4D quantum space
  - Phase correlation between quantum states
  - Coherence product weighting
- Prunes relationships below strength threshold (0.3)

### Redis Integration
- Persistent storage for LTM patterns
- Automatic serialization/deserialization of quantum states
- Bulk operations for pattern loading/storing
- Pattern relationship persistence

